1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Listen, practice, speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,400
Hello and welcome back to Business English Podcast.

3
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,400
Hi everyone.

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,480
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

5
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:22,480
I'm Daniel.

6
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,640
And I'm Sophia.

7
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:26,800
And we're really happy you're here learning with us today.

8
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:32,800
On this channel, we help you speak English naturally and confidently through real conversations,

9
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,600
practical examples, and everyday workplace situations.

10
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:41,920
That's right, and today we have a very modern and practical topic that is becoming more and

11
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:44,920
more important in workplaces around the world.

12
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:49,760
Yes, today's topic is how to use AI in business meetings.

13
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:52,840
This is something many professionals are curious about.

14
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:58,000
AI tools are becoming part of daily work and meetings are one of the main areas where

15
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,200
people are starting to use them.

16
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:05,720
Exactly, but many people are not sure how to use AI effectively during meetings.

17
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:11,400
They might worry about sounding unnatural, relying too much on technology, or not knowing

18
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,400
when to use it.

19
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,920
That's a great point.

20
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:17,960
AI is a tool, not a replacement for communication.

21
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:22,600
The goal is to use it to support your ideas, not replace your thinking.

22
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:28,320
So today, we're going to simulate a realistic and detailed conversation between two colleagues

23
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:34,920
discussing how they use AI in meetings, including practical examples and real situations.

24
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:39,800
will also demonstrate useful English phrases that you can use when talking about AI in a

25
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,640
professional environment.

26
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:47,040
And remember, the goal is to sound clear, confident, and natural while using AI as a

27
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,040
support tool.

28
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,040
Exactly.

29
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,680
So, let's begin.

30
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,120
Imagine this situation.

31
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:56,160
Sophia and I are colleagues preparing for an important business meeting.

32
00:01:56,160 --> 00:02:02,000
Yes, and we're discussing how to use AI tools effectively before, during, and after

33
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
the meeting.

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,440
Alright, let's start the conversation.

35
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:09,240
Hey Sophia, do you have a few minutes to prepare for tomorrow's meeting?

36
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,240
Of course, Daniel.

37
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:12,920
I was actually just reviewing the agenda.

38
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:16,280
It looks like an important meeting with the senior management team.

39
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,600
Yes, it is.

40
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:21,600
I was thinking we could use some AI tools to help us prepare more efficiently.

41
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,560
That's a great idea.

42
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:27,920
I've been using AI more frequently in my workflow, but I'd love to hear how you

43
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,960
plan to use it for this meeting.

44
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:34,960
Well, first, I used an AI tool to summarize last week's meeting notes.

45
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:39,160
It helped me quickly understand the key points and action items.

46
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,880
That's very useful.

47
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:44,240
Sometimes reading long meeting notes can take a lot of time.

48
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,240
Exactly.

49
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:49,920
The AI summarized everything into a few clear bullet points, which made it easier to

50
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,680
focus on what matters.

51
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,800
I like that.

52
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:55,400
Did you verify the summary for accuracy?

53
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,400
Yes.

54
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,280
I always double-check important details.

55
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:02,120
AI is helpful, but it's important to review the output.

56
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,440
That's a very responsible approach.

57
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:07,720
So how else can we use AI before the meeting?

58
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:11,960
Another thing I did was ask the AI to suggest possible questions

59
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,680
that management might ask during the meeting.

60
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:18,280
That's interesting. What kind of questions did it suggest?

61
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:22,440
For example, it suggested questions about project timelines,

62
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:25,400
budget efficiency, and potential risks.

63
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:27,880
That's actually very realistic.

64
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:31,880
Those are exactly the types of questions managers usually ask.

65
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:34,880
Yes, and it helped me prepare answers in advance.

66
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:37,880
That's a great way to build confidence.

67
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:40,880
I think preparation is one of the best uses of AI.

68
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:46,880
I agree. I also used AI to help me organize my presentation points more clearly.

69
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:47,880
How did you do that?

70
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:54,880
I gave the AI a rough outline of my ideas, and it helped me structure them into a logical flow.

71
00:03:54,880 --> 00:04:00,880
That sounds very helpful, especially when you have many ideas but need to present them clearly.

72
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:05,880
Exactly. It helped me avoid repetition and made my message more concise.

73
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:10,880
I think that's one of the biggest advantages of AI. It helps you communicate more clearly.

74
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:15,880
Yes. Now let's talk about how we can use AI during the meeting itself.

75
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:19,880
That's where it gets really interesting. What are your thoughts?

76
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:25,260
During the meeting, we can use AI note-taking tools to automatically record and summarize

77
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:26,660
the discussion.

78
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:28,700
That would be very useful.

79
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:32,860
Sometimes it's hard to listen, speak, and take notes at the same time.

80
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,860
Exactly.

81
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:38,020
With AI handling the notes, we can focus more on the conversation.

82
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:40,580
That improves engagement and communication.

83
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:45,820
Yes, but again, we should review the notes afterward to ensure accuracy.

84
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:46,980
Definitely.

85
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,800
What about real-time support?

86
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:51,040
Can AI help during the meeting itself?

87
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,040
Yes.

88
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:58,720
For example, if we need quick data or definitions, we can use AI to find information instantly.

89
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:01,360
That can save time instead of searching manually.

90
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,360
Right.

91
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:07,520
For example, if someone asks about market trends, we can quickly check relevant data.

92
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,960
That makes you look prepared and informed.

93
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:10,960
Exactly.

94
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:15,040
But we should be careful not to rely on AI too much during the meeting.

95
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,040
I agree.

96
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:19,640
It's important to maintain eye contact and active participation.

97
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:23,160
Yes, communication should always come first.

98
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:26,220
Another idea is using AI to help with language.

99
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:31,840
For example, if someone is not a native English speaker, AI can suggest better phrasing.

100
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,200
That's a great point.

101
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:35,960
It can help improve clarity and confidence.

102
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:40,120
But again, it should be used as support, not a replacement.

103
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,120
Exactly.

104
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:44,840
Now let's talk about how AI can help us after the meeting.

105
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:47,840
I think this is one of the most powerful uses.

106
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:51,340
AI can summarize the meeting and highlight action items.

107
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:54,640
Yes, and it can even organize tasks by priority.

108
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,240
That's very helpful for productivity.

109
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:00,560
I also use AI to draft follow-up emails.

110
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,440
That saves a lot of time.

111
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,560
Yes, I just provide key points

112
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:07,800
and the AI creates a professional email draft.

113
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:10,120
Do you edit the email before sending it?

114
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:10,960
Always.

115
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:14,040
I personalize it and make sure the tone is appropriate.

116
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:17,680
That's important. Communication should still feel human.

117
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:22,920
Exactly. AI helps with efficiency, but we add the personal touch.

118
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,840
Let's talk about a real example.

119
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:28,320
Can you describe a meeting where you used AI successfully?

120
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:33,760
Sure. Last month, I had a meeting with a client about improving their marketing strategy.

121
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,960
What did you do?

122
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:40,880
Before the meeting, I used an AI tool to analyze the client's website and generate insights.

123
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,260
That sounds advanced.

124
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:44,220
What kind of insights did you get?

125
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:46,620
It highlighted areas for improvement,

126
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:49,700
such as website speed and content clarity.

127
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:51,820
That must have impressed the client.

128
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:54,780
Yes, it helped me provide valuable suggestions

129
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:55,820
during the meeting.

130
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:57,940
Did you use AI during the meeting?

131
00:06:57,940 --> 00:07:01,460
Yes, I used a note-taking tool to capture the discussion.

132
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:02,900
And after the meeting?

133
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:04,980
I used AI to summarize the meeting

134
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:06,900
and create a follow-up plan.

135
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,900
That's a complete workflow, very efficient.

136
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:12,940
Yes, it saved time and improved quality.

137
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:14,820
Were there any challenges?

138
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:18,940
Yes, sometimes the AI suggestions were too generic.

139
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:20,100
That can happen.

140
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:23,220
So I had to refine them and make them more specific.

141
00:07:23,220 --> 00:07:25,620
That's where human judgment is important.

142
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:26,700
Exactly.

143
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:28,580
AI provides a starting point,

144
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:30,700
but we make the final decisions.

145
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,660
Let's talk about common mistakes

146
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,620
when using AI in meetings.

147
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:36,860
One mistake is relying on AI

148
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:39,180
without understanding the content.

149
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:40,660
That can be risky.

150
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:43,620
Yes, you must understand what you're presenting.

151
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:47,620
Another mistake is overusing AI during conversations.

152
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:50,740
That can make communication feel unnatural.

153
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:51,580
Exactly.

154
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:54,100
Meetings are about human interaction.

155
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:58,060
Another mistake is not checking AI-generated information.

156
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,740
That's very important.

157
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:01,220
Accuracy matters.

158
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,420
Absolutely.

159
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:04,580
Now let's practice some useful phrases

160
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:06,420
for using AI in meetings.

161
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:07,380
Great idea.

162
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:12,340
You can say, I used an AI tool to summarize our previous discussion.

163
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:18,380
Or you can say, I asked an AI system to analyze this data and provide insights.

164
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:23,420
Another example is, let me quickly check this information using an AI tool.

165
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:29,500
And you can say, I've prepared a draft using AI and I'd like to refine it with your input.

166
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:32,380
These phrases sound professional and natural.

167
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:35,860
Yes, they show that you are using technology effectively.

168
00:08:35,860 --> 00:08:39,340
Now let's continue the conversation with a deeper scenario.

169
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:40,100
Sure.

170
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:42,740
I'm imagining we are in the meeting now.

171
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:44,740
OK, I'll act as the manager.

172
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:47,140
Daniel, can you summarize the key points

173
00:08:47,140 --> 00:08:48,500
from last week's meeting?

174
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:51,940
Yes, I used an AI tool to review the notes.

175
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:55,780
The main points were improving efficiency, reducing costs,

176
00:08:55,780 --> 00:08:58,180
and enhancing customer experience.

177
00:08:58,180 --> 00:08:59,420
That's clear.

178
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:01,100
What about the action items?

179
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:04,220
The key action items include updating the system,

180
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:07,580
reviewing the budget in conducting customer surveys.

181
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:09,940
Excellent, that's very organized.

182
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:10,780
Thank you.

183
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:13,260
Now let's return to our podcast discussion.

184
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:14,100
Sure.

185
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:17,420
This example shows how AI can support communication

186
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:18,880
without replacing it.

187
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:22,140
Exactly, it enhances clarity and efficiency.

188
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:25,380
Before we finish, let's give our listeners a challenge.

189
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,220
Good idea.

190
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:28,060
Think about your next meeting.

191
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:30,380
How can you use AI to prepare?

192
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:33,420
Maybe summarize notes, generate ideas,

193
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:35,220
or organize your thoughts.

194
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:38,740
Then think about how you can use AI after the meeting.

195
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:40,980
For example, writing follow-up emails

196
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,980
or summarizing action points.

197
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:47,100
Practice using simple English to explain your use of AI.

198
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:50,180
The more you practice, the more confident you will become.

199
00:09:50,180 --> 00:09:52,340
Thank you so much for listening today.

200
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:54,300
Keep practicing, keep improving,

201
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:56,100
and keep speaking English.

202
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:57,620
See you in the next episode.

203
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:58,460
Goodbye, everyone.

204
