On this channel, we help you speak English

211
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:16,260
naturally and confidently through real conversations,

212
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:19,780
practical examples, and everyday workplace situations.

213
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:20,620
That's right.

214
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,460
And today, we're going to talk about a very modern

215
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:26,220
and important topic that many professionals

216
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,300
are interested in.

217
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:31,900
Yes, today's topic is how to use AI in business meetings.

218
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:35,500
This is becoming a very valuable skill in today's workplace.

219
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:36,700
Absolutely.

220
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:43,700
More and more companies are using AI tools to improve productivity, communication, and decision making.

221
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:51,400
And in meetings, AI can help with note-taking, summarizing discussions, analyzing data, and even suggesting ideas.

222
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,500
Exactly.

223
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:59,600
But many people are not sure how to talk about using AI in English, especially in professional situations.

224
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:05,100
So, today we're going to have a realistic conversation where we show you how to naturally

225
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:07,640
discuss using AI in meetings.

226
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:12,480
We'll use simple, clear business English, and we'll include practical examples that

227
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:14,720
you can use in your own workplace.

228
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,720
Great.

229
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,720
Let's begin.

230
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:21,000
So, Sophia, have you started using AI tools in your meetings at work?

231
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,880
Yes, actually I have.

232
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:27,240
Over the past few months, our team has started integrating AI into many of our

233
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,480
weekly meetings.

234
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:31,880
That sounds interesting. Can you tell me more about how you use it?

235
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:38,480
Sure. One of the main ways we use AI is for automatic meeting summaries. After every meeting,

236
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:41,880
the AI tool generates a summary of the key points.

237
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:43,740
That must save a lot of time.

238
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:49,540
It really does. Before, someone had to manually take notes and sometimes important details

239
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:50,540
were missed.

240
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:56,120
Yes, I've experienced that before. Manual note-taking can be stressful during meetings.

241
00:11:56,120 --> 00:12:02,120
Exactly. Now we can focus more on the discussion instead of worrying about writing everything down.

242
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:08,120
That's a big advantage. So how do you usually introduce AI usage in a meeting?

243
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:13,120
Usually, at the beginning of the meeting, I say something like, just to let everyone know,

244
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:18,120
we'll be using an AI tool today to record and summarize our discussion.

245
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:20,120
That sounds clear and professional.

246
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:25,120
Yes, it's important to inform everyone, especially because of privacy and transparency.

247
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:30,480
That's a very good point. People should always know when AI tools are being used.

248
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:34,560
Absolutely. Communication is key in professional environments.

249
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:38,720
Besides summaries, what other ways do you use AI in meetings?

250
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:45,280
Another common use is generating action items. After the meeting, the AI identifies tasks

251
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:48,800
and assigns responsibilities. That sounds very efficient.

252
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:53,760
It is. For example, instead of manually deciding who does what,

253
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:57,760
the AI suggests action points based on the conversation.

254
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,160
Can you give me an example?

255
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:00,060
Sure.

256
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:04,260
Let's say during a meeting we discuss launching a new product.

257
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:07,360
The AI might generate action items like

258
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:10,460
marketing team to prepare campaign strategy

259
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:13,560
or sales team to contact key clients.

260
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:15,060
That's very helpful.

261
00:13:15,060 --> 00:13:16,860
It ensures nothing is forgotten.

262
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:17,860
Exactly.

263
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:20,260
It improves accountability and clarity.

264
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:23,460
How do people in your team feel about using AI?

265
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:28,820
At first, some people were unsure, they were worried about accuracy and reliability.

266
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:33,300
That's understandable. New technology can sometimes feel uncomfortable.

267
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:38,420
Yes, but after using it for a few weeks, most people became more confident.

268
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:41,060
Did you have to explain how the AI works?

269
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:47,300
Yes, I did. During one meeting, I explained the AI tool uses speech recognition and

270
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:50,580
natural language processing to understand our discussion.

271
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,340
That sounds quite technical.

272
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:55,140
It does, but I try to keep it simple.

273
00:13:55,140 --> 00:14:00,820
I usually add, it basically listens to the conversation and identifies key points.

274
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:02,900
That makes it easier to understand.

275
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:06,500
Exactly. Simple explanations are always better in meetings.

276
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:10,740
Have you ever used AI during the meeting itself, not just after?

277
00:14:10,740 --> 00:14:14,740
Yes, sometimes we use AI for real-time suggestions.

278
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:16,020
What do you mean by that?

279
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:22,260
For example, during brainstorming sessions, the AI can suggest ideas based on the discussion.

280
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:24,260
That sounds very advanced.

281
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:26,260
It is, but it's very useful.

282
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:30,260
If the team is stuck, the AI can provide new perspectives.

283
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:31,260
Can you give an example?

284
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,260
Sure.

285
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:37,260
During a marketing meeting, we were discussing ways to improve customer engagement.

286
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:42,260
The AI suggested using personalized email campaigns and interactive content.

287
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:44,260
That's impressive.

288
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:46,260
Yes, and it helped us think in new ways.

289
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:49,260
How do you introduce that during a meeting?

290
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:54,620
I usually say, let's use the AI tool to generate some additional ideas.

291
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:56,020
That sounds very natural.

292
00:14:56,020 --> 00:15:00,480
Yes, and it encourages collaboration between humans and technology.

293
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,980
That's a great way to put it.

294
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:02,980
Thank you.

295
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:07,700
I think the key is to treat AI as a support tool, not a replacement.

296
00:15:07,700 --> 00:15:09,580
That's an important mindset.

297
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:10,580
Absolutely.

298
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:14,180
AI should enhance human decision-making, not replace it.

299
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:17,620
Have you ever faced challenges when using AI in meetings?

300
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:19,100
Yes, definitely.

301
00:15:19,100 --> 00:15:20,820
What kind of challenges?

302
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:23,260
One challenge is accuracy.

303
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:27,140
Sometimes the AI misunderstands certain words or accents.

304
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,500
That can be a problem.

305
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:33,180
Yes, especially in international teams where people have different accents.

306
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:34,420
How do you handle that?

307
00:15:34,420 --> 00:15:38,740
We always review the AI generated summary before we finalize it.

308
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:39,900
That's a good approach.

309
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:46,140
Yes, I usually say, please review the summary to ensure accuracy before we finalize it.

310
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:47,900
That sounds very professional.

311
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:48,900
Thank you.

312
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:50,640
to maintain quality.

313
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:51,980
Any other challenges?

314
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:55,060
Another challenge is over-reliance on AI.

315
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:55,940
What do you mean?

316
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:58,980
Sometimes people trust the AI too much

317
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:00,740
and stop thinking critically.

318
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:02,660
That's a very interesting point.

319
00:16:02,660 --> 00:16:05,380
Yes, so I often remind the team,

320
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:07,540
AI is a tool to support us,

321
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:10,180
but we still need to use our own judgment.

322
00:16:10,180 --> 00:16:11,780
That's excellent advice.

323
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:12,620
Thank you.

324
00:16:12,620 --> 00:16:14,420
Balance is very important.

325
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:17,720
Have you used AI for presentations during meetings?

326
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:18,880
Yes, we have.

327
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:19,960
How does that work?

328
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:22,680
The AI helps create presentation slides

329
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:24,360
based on meeting topics.

330
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:26,840
That must save a lot of preparation time.

331
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:27,680
It does.

332
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:31,080
For example, I can say, generate a presentation

333
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:33,680
based on our quarterly performance discussion.

334
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:35,880
And it creates slides automatically?

335
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:39,040
Yes, with key points, charts, and summaries.

336
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:40,440
That's very efficient.

337
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:43,440
It is, but we still review and edit the slides

338
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,640
before presenting.

339
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:47,480
Of course, human review is still necessary.

340
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,400
Exactly.

341
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:52,080
How about using AI for data analysis in meetings?

342
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:54,280
That's another powerful use.

343
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:57,360
AI can quickly analyze large amounts of data

344
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,800
and present insights.

345
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:01,440
That must be very helpful for decision-making.

346
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:02,240
It is.

347
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:05,000
Instead of spending hours analyzing data,

348
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,040
we can get insights in minutes.

349
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,200
How do you talk about that in a meeting?

350
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:12,880
I might say, let's use AI to analyze the data

351
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:14,480
and identify trends.

352
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:16,520
That sounds clear and professional.

353
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:22,240
Yes, and it helps the team focus on interpreting the results instead of processing the data.

354
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,760
That's a big advantage.

355
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:24,760
Absolutely.

356
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:28,800
Do you think AI will become standard in all business meetings?

357
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,200
I believe so.

358
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:32,280
It's already becoming very common.

359
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:34,040
I agree.

360
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:36,080
Technology is changing the way we work.

361
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:41,640
Yes, and professionals who understand how to use AI will have a strong advantage.

362
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:42,640
That's true.

363
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:44,680
It's an important skill for the future.

364
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,680
Definitely.

365
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:47,860
Let's imagine a situation.

366
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:51,660
You are in a meeting and you want to suggest using AI.

367
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:52,660
What would you say?

368
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:59,060
I might say, to improve efficiency, I suggest we use an AI tool to capture key points and

369
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:00,380
action items.

370
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:02,060
That sounds very natural.

371
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:03,060
Thank you.

372
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:05,580
And if someone is unsure about using AI?

373
00:18:05,580 --> 00:18:10,900
I would respond, we can review the output together to ensure accuracy and make any

374
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:12,700
necessary adjustments.

375
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:13,700
That's reassuring.

376
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,860
Yes, it helps build trust.

377
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:18,700
What about ending a meeting with AI support?

378
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:21,500
At the end, I might say the AI tool

379
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:23,860
will generate a summary and action items,

380
00:18:23,860 --> 00:18:26,020
which I will share with everyone shortly.

381
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:27,820
That sounds very professional.

382
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:28,660
Thank you.

383
00:18:28,660 --> 00:18:31,260
Clear communication is always important.

384
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:34,220
Before we finish, what is your biggest tip

385
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:36,200
for using AI in meetings?

386
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:40,020
My biggest tip is to keep it simple and transparent.

387
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:43,260
Always explain how you're using AI and why.

388
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:44,620
That's great advice.

389
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:46,740
And always review the results.

390
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:48,980
Don't rely on AI blindly.

391
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:50,180
Excellent point.

392
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:51,220
What about you?

393
00:18:51,220 --> 00:18:53,580
Do you plan to use AI in your meetings?

394
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:55,060
Yes, definitely.

395
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:58,140
After this conversation, I feel more confident about it.

396
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,260
That's great to hear.

397
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:01,260
I think I'll start with simple tools

398
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:02,780
like meeting summaries.

399
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:04,220
That's a good starting point.

400
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:07,380
Then gradually explore more advanced features.

401
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:08,220
Exactly.

402
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:10,500
Step by step is the best approach.

403
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:13,180
Well, this has been a very useful discussion.

404
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:16,220
Yes, I hope our listeners found it helpful too.

405
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:18,940
Before we end, here's a question for you.

406
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,900
Yes, think about this.

407
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:24,220
How would you use AI in your next business meeting?

408
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:28,060
Try to answer in English, practice phrases like suggesting,

409
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:30,220
explaining, and summarizing.

410
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:33,380
The more you practice, the more confident you will become.

411
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,580
Thank you so much for listening today.

412
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:38,940
Keep practicing your English and keep learning new skills.

413
00:19:38,940 --> 00:19:43,140
And remember, communication is the key to success in business.

414
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:44,340
Goodbye, everyone.

415
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:54,280
See you next time.

416
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:55,280
Hello, everyone.

417
00:19:55,280 --> 00:20:00,360
Welcome back to the podcast where we help you communicate more confidently in professional

418
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:01,860
situations.

419
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:03,100
And hello, everyone.

420
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,620
We're very happy you are here with us today.

421
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:11,840
In this podcast, we focus on practical English you can use in meetings, presentations, interviews,

422
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:14,200
and everyday business communication.

423
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,200
That's right.

424
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:19,080
And today, we have a very modern and highly practical topic.

425
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:20,080
Yes.

426
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:24,000
Next topic is how to use AI in business meetings.

427
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:29,220
This is becoming an essential skill because many companies are now integrating AI into

428
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:30,960
their daily workflows.

429
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:31,960
Exactly.

430
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:37,360
But while many people know about AI, they are not always sure how to use it effectively

431
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,880
during meetings.

432
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:45,200
So today, we're going to give you a comprehensive and detailed conversation with real practical

433
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:46,200
examples.

434
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:52,680
And we will simulate realistic workplace situations so you can learn natural English expressions.

435
00:20:52,680 --> 00:21:00,200
We will talk about using AI before meetings, during meetings, and after meetings, all through conversation.

436
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:05,080
And we will also discuss challenges, mistakes, and best practices.

437
00:21:05,080 --> 00:21:06,280
All right, let's begin.

438
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:12,600
So, Speaker 1, I heard that your company recently started using AI tools in meetings.

439
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:13,320
Is that correct?

440
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,480
Yes, that's correct.

441
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:21,320
Over the past six months, we've gradually introduced AI tools into our meeting processes.

442
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:26,440
That sounds like a big change. What motivated your company to start using AI?

443
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:32,440
The main reason was efficiency. We noticed that meetings were taking too long and sometimes

444
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:36,920
they were not very productive. That's a common problem in many organizations.

445
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:43,480
Exactly. People often spent too much time preparing, taking notes, and writing follow-up

446
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:47,480
So AI was introduced to solve those problems?

447
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:51,480
Yes. The goal was to save time, improve clarity,

448
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:54,480
and make meetings more results-oriented.

449
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:59,480
Let's start with the preparation phase. How do you use AI before a meeting?

450
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:03,480
Before a meeting, AI helps us in several ways.

451
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:07,480
One of the most useful features is agenda creation.

452
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:09,480
Can you explain how that works?

453
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:15,960
Sure. Instead of writing the agenda manually, I give the AI a short description of the meeting.

454
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:21,240
For example, I might say, create an agenda for a product launch planning meeting.

455
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:24,040
And the AI generates a full agenda?

456
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:29,960
Yes, it usually creates a structured agenda with sections like objectives, discussion topics,

457
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:32,760
time allocation, and expected outcomes.

458
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,760
That sounds very organized.

459
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:39,000
It is, and it also helps ensure that the meeting stays focused.

460
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:42,280
Do you ever modify the AI-generated agenda?

461
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:43,880
Yes, always.

462
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:45,520
I treat it as a draft.

463
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:49,360
I review it and adjust it based on our specific needs.

464
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,840
That's a good approach.

465
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:54,200
AI should support not replace human thinking.

466
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,400
Exactly.

467
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,840
What about research?

468
00:22:56,840 --> 00:22:59,560
Does AI help with gathering information?

469
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:02,280
Yes, that's another major advantage.

470
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:06,840
Before meetings, we often need to review reports, emails, or data.

471
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:08,760
That can take a lot of time.

472
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:14,040
It does, but with AI we can upload documents and ask for summaries.

473
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:16,040
Can you give a real example?

474
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:19,960
Sure. Last month we had a meeting about customer satisfaction.

475
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:22,280
We had hundreds of survey responses.

476
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:24,120
That sounds overwhelming.

477
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:28,680
It was, but we used AI to summarize the responses.

478
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:31,880
It identified key themes like slow delivery,

479
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:35,000
product quality, and customer support issues.

480
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,840
That must have saved hours of work.

481
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:42,840
Yes, and it allowed us to focus directly on the main issues during the meeting.

482
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:47,840
That's very practical. Now let's talk about using AI during the meeting itself.

483
00:23:47,840 --> 00:23:52,840
During the meeting, AI plays an even more active role.

484
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:54,840
What is the most common use?

485
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:57,840
The most common use is automatic note-taking.

486
00:23:57,840 --> 00:23:59,840
How does that work exactly?

487
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:03,840
The AI tool records the meeting and generates real-time notes.

488
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:07,840
It identifies key points, decisions, and action items.

489
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:10,840
So participants don't need to take notes manually?

490
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:15,840
Exactly. This allows everyone to focus fully on the discussion.

491
00:24:15,840 --> 00:24:17,840
That must improve engagement.

492
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:21,840
Yes, people are more present and active in the conversation.

493
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:24,840
Does the AI also organize the notes?

494
00:24:24,840 --> 00:24:30,840
Yes, it usually organizes them into sections like discussion points, decisions, and next steps.

495
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:32,840
That sounds very useful for follow-up.

496
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:34,840
It is.

497
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:36,840
What about language support?

498
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:41,840
AI is very helpful for communication, especially in international teams.

499
00:24:41,840 --> 00:24:43,840
Can you explain that?

500
00:24:43,840 --> 00:24:47,840
For example, some team members are not native English speakers.

501
00:24:47,840 --> 00:24:51,840
AI can help them rephrase sentences or check grammar before they speak.

502
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:53,840
That can increase confidence.

503
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:59,840
Exactly. It reduces anxiety and helps people express their ideas more clearly.

504
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:03,120
Does AI also help with real-time translation?

505
00:25:03,120 --> 00:25:06,520
Yes, some tools provide live translation.

506
00:25:06,520 --> 00:25:07,880
That's amazing.

507
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:10,840
It is especially useful in global companies

508
00:25:10,840 --> 00:25:13,440
where team numbers speak different languages.

509
00:25:13,440 --> 00:25:15,520
Let's talk about decision-making.

510
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:18,520
Can AI support decisions during meetings?

511
00:25:18,520 --> 00:25:22,840
Yes, AI can analyze data quickly and provide insights.

512
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:25,040
Can you give a practical example?

513
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:25,840
Sure.

514
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:28,480
During a sales meeting, we needed to decide

515
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:30,600
which market to focus on.

516
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:32,440
That's an important decision.

517
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:37,400
Yes, we asked AI to analyze sales data from different regions.

518
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:38,920
And what did it do?

519
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:40,920
It identified trends and suggested

520
00:25:40,920 --> 00:25:44,320
that one region had the highest growth potential.

521
00:25:44,320 --> 00:25:46,200
That's very helpful.

522
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:48,720
Yes, but we still discussed it as a team

523
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:50,880
before making the final decision.

524
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:52,320
That's important.

525
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:55,480
AI should support decisions, not make them.

526
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:59,240
Exactly. Human judgment is still essential.

527
00:25:59,240 --> 00:26:01,080
